WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.400
Shine a lamp on pondweed in water,
and bubbles of oxygen stream from it.

2
00:00:05.450 --> 00:00:08.920
Move the lamp closer, and
the bubbles come faster.

3
00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:11.980
Then, at some point, nothing changes.

4
00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:15.490
However bright the light,
the rate stays flat.

5
00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:18.140
A greenhouse grower sees the same thing.

6
00:00:18.190 --> 00:00:21.610
Brighter lamps no longer
make the crop grow faster.

7
00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:24.290
So what should the grower change instead?

8
00:00:24.340 --> 00:00:28.540
In this mission, you'll find out what the
flat part of the curve is really telling

9
00:00:28.590 --> 00:00:29.270
you.

10
00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:31.790
Then you'll work through
a table of crop data,

11
00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:34.240
and plan the grower's next move.

12
00:00:34.290 --> 00:00:37.380
Your mission: decide what
the grower should change,

13
00:00:37.430 --> 00:00:39.390
instead of fitting brighter lamps.
